#N canvas 0 50 1040 1280 12;
#X text 30 16 =^..^=   b3~   version 1 (2026)   sofia vallejo budziszewski   iem kug graz austria;
#X text 30 46 b-3 style tonewheel organ;
#X text 30 86 nine drawbars with single-trigger percussion key click scanner vibrato and chorus overdrive and a rotary speaker with horn and drum. up to 32 voices., f 110;
#X text 30 146 --- how it was made ---;
#X text 30 190 each voice is nine sine partials (the drawbar footages) that add up. percussion is a second or third harmonic with its own decay., f 110;
#X text 30 240 key click is a short noise burst at note on. vibrato and chorus is a modulated delay line and the rotary is a horn and a drum with their own speeds and inertia., f 110;
#X text 30 290 it is an additive model and not a tonewheel simulation so there is no crosstalk or leakage., f 110;
#X text 30 330 --- how to use ---;
#X text 30 374 1  open the engine page below and turn dsp on, f 110;
#X text 30 404 2  play a midi keyboard or click chord on, f 110;
#X text 30 434 3  open the parameters page and move any control or open presets and step through the sounds, f 110;
#X text 30 464 4  everything is a message: see the messages page for the full list and the examples page for patches to copy, f 110;
#X text 30 524 try:  pull the drawbars with the vertical sliders: d8 is the fundamental and d16 is one octave below, f 110;
#X text 30 554 try:  turn perc on: the percussion fires only on the first key of a phrase as on the real organ, f 110;
#X text 30 584 try:  switch leslie between slow and fast: the rotor speeds up and slows down with inertia, f 110;
#X text 30 628 --- common problems ---;
#X text 30 672 no sound: turn dsp on in the engine page and check the volume slider. the synth needs a note: click chord on or play a midi key, f 110;
#X text 30 722 nothing changes after a rebuild: pd keeps the old external in memory so close every patch and restart pd, f 110;
#X text 30 752 a note is stuck: send panic. a missing note off from a midi device is the usual cause, f 110;
#X text 30 782 unknown parameter in the console: names are exact and lowercase so send params to print them all, f 110;
#X text 30 812 a bank file is not found: save and load names are relative to the folder of this patch, f 110;
#X text 30 842 the sliders do not move when you change a preset: the object must be created with the same name as in the boxes. default name is the object name, f 110;
#X text 30 892 clicks or dropouts: raise the audio buffer in the pd audio settings or lower the voice count in the creation argument, f 110;
#X text 30 942 no percussion: it needs perc on and it only fires on the first key of a phrase so release all keys between tests, f 110;
#X text 30 992 the sound is too quiet: raise d8 first because drawbars add up and many open bars are loud, f 110;
#X text 30 1036 --- click a box to open that page ---;
#N canvas 0 50 900 1242 presets 0;
#X text 30 16 presets: factory sounds are stored as plain text and every control above is a message. click a box to load that sound, f 100;
#X text 30 66 --- factory presets ---;
#X msg 30 110 \; b3 preset 0;
#X text 250 112 0  jazz 888;
#X msg 30 164 \; b3 preset 1;
#X text 250 166 1  full organ;
#X msg 30 218 \; b3 preset 2;
#X text 250 220 2  gospel;
#X msg 30 272 \; b3 preset 3;
#X text 250 274 3  rock;
#X msg 30 326 \; b3 preset 4;
#X text 250 328 4  mellow flute;
#X msg 30 380 \; b3 preset 5;
#X text 250 382 5  church;
#X msg 30 434 \; b3 preset 6;
#X text 250 436 6  pad organ;
#X msg 460 110 \; b3 preset 7;
#X text 680 112 7  percussive;
#X msg 460 164 \; b3 preset 8;
#X text 680 166 8  ballad;
#X msg 460 218 \; b3 preset 9;
#X text 680 220 9  reed buzz;
#X msg 460 272 \; b3 preset 10;
#X text 680 274 10  soft pad 4;
#X msg 460 326 \; b3 preset 11;
#X text 680 328 11  third perc;
#X msg 460 380 \; b3 preset 12;
#X text 680 382 12  dry organ;
#X msg 460 434 \; b3 preset 13;
#X text 680 436 13  thin lead;
#X text 30 508 --- now playing ---;
#X symbolatom 30 552 20 0 0 0 - b3-name - 0;
#X floatatom 230 552 4 0 0 0 - b3-index - 0;
#X text 340 554 name and number (minus one means edited);
#X msg 30 596 \; b3 next;
#X msg 142 596 \; b3 prev;
#X msg 254 596 \; b3 mutate 0.3;
#X text 30 656 next and prev step through the presets and wrap around. mutate varies the current sound by a random amount from 0 to 1, f 100;
#X text 30 706 --- morph between two sounds ---;
#X msg 30 750 \; b3 A;
#X msg 118 750 \; b3 B;
#X text 206 752 a and b remember the current sound;
#X text 30 812 morph;
#X obj 110 810 hsl 300 18 0 1 0 0 b3-morph b3-morph-r empty -2 -8 0 12 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X text 30 854 load one preset and press a then load another and press b then move the morph slider. every parameter blends smoothly between the two, f 100;
#X text 30 904 --- your own user bank ---;
#X msg 30 948 \; b3 store mysound;
#X msg 214 948 \; b3 save my.bank;
#X msg 390 948 \; b3 load my.bank;
#X text 30 1008 store keeps the current sound after the factory presets. save writes the user bank to a text file next to this patch and load adds the sounds from a text file, f 100;
#X text 30 1058 --- presets with stash ---;
#X text 30 1102 every slider in the parameters page sends to b3-name and listens on b3-name-r so the stash library can store and morph whole scenes: create [stash/bank b3] and send it a scan message for a saved copy of the parameters page. this follows the stash naming rules but has not been tested together yet, f 100;
#X restore 30 1080 pd presets;
#X text 30 1114 all sounds and morph, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1500 902 parameters 0;
#X text 30 16 every control here is also a message: set name value with values from 0 to 1. switches take the step number shown under each one, f 120;
